            <ArticleTitle>Cyclic benzamidines as orally efficacious NR2B-selective NMDA receptor antagonists.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3997-4000</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A novel series of cyclic benzamidines was synthesized and shown to exhibit NR2B-subtype selective NMDA antagonist activity. Compound 29 is orally active in a carrageenan-induced rat hyperalgesia model of pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
